    <innerclass refid="classend_1_1_window" prot="public">end::Window</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceend">end</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Config-reactive DocumentWindow for END. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classend_1_1_window" kindref="compound">end::Window</ref> extends <ref refid="classjam_1_1Window" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">jam::Window</ref> with listener-driven style application. It follows the same architectural pattern as ProcessorChain::parameters: a <ref refid="structjam_1_1Function_1_1Map" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">jam::Function::Map</ref> keyed on <ref refid="classjuce_1_1Identifier" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">juce::Identifier</ref> stores one typed callable per config property, registered as <computeroutput>add&lt;juce::ValueTree&gt;</computeroutput>. Each callable receives the pre-resolved VT node (WINDOW node or BLUR_STYLE node) and reads its one property directly from it. <ref refid="unionNode" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">Node</ref> resolution lives exclusively in applyStyleFor(), which is the single source of tree navigation. valueTreePropertyChanged() forwards to applyStyleFor(); setStyle() calls applyStyleFor() once per registered property to apply the initial config state.</para>
<para>Window also inherits <ref refid="structjam_1_1ValueTree_1_1Component" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">jam::ValueTree::Component</ref> (TYPE = IDtype::window). Its owned node is grafted into <ref refid="classend_1_1_model" kindref="compound">end::Model</ref>&apos;s root tree via a <ref refid="classjam_1_1ValueTree_1_1Attachment" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">jam::ValueTree::Attachment</ref> owned by <ref refid="classend_1_1_application" kindref="compound">end::Application</ref>. The WINDOW node starts empty — properties are written by their authors (View::resized for width/height, zoom actions for zoom, etc.).</para>
<para>Config tree shape navigated by the dispatcher: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">CONFIG</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>DISPLAY<sp/><sp/>(IDtype::display)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>WINDOW<sp/><sp/>(IDtype::window)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>colour,<sp/>blur_radius,<sp/>always_on_top,<sp/>buttons,<sp/>width,<sp/>height</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>BLUR_STYLE<sp/><sp/>(IDtype::blurStyle)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>mac,<sp/>win</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
